--- Completion 1 ---
To count the number of chairs in the scene, we will use the Object Detector Tool to detect chairs. We will set the label list to ['chair'] and then loop through the detected objects to count the number of chairs.

<command>
```python
from object_detector import Object_Detector_Tool

# Initialize the Object Detector Tool with the appropriate parameters
detector_tool = Object_Detector_Tool()

# Get the label list to be detected
label_list = ['chair']

# Execute the detection
result = detector_tool.execute(image_path='image_path', labels=label_list, model_size='tiny', save_object=True, saved_image_path='detected_objects')

# Count the number of detected chairs
chairs_count = sum([detect['bbox'][0]['x'] + detect['bbox'][0]['y'] for detect in result.get('detected_objects', [])])

print("Number of chairs detected:", chairs_count)
```
